  "question": {
    "text": "<strong>Paragraph:</strong>\nRead the following passage and answer the questions.\nFor every function $f(x)$ which is twice differentiable, these will be good approximation of $\\int_a^b f(x) d x \\cong\\left(\\frac{b-a}{2}\\right)\\{f(a)+f(b)\\}$. Now, if we take $c=\\frac{a+b}{2}$, then using above again, we get $\\int_a^b f(x) d x=\\int_a^c f(x) d x+\\int_c^b f(x) d x \\cong \\frac{b-a}{4}\\{f(a)+f(b)+2 f(c)\\}$ and so on.\nWe get approximation for value of $\\int_a^b f(x) d x$.<strong>Question:</strong>\nGood approximation of $\\int_0^{\\pi / 2} \\sin x d x$, is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "lpcSk",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{4}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "XVep8",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{4}(\\sqrt{2}+1)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "7wEPb",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{8}(\\sqrt{2}+1)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "K9Xnl",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{8}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\int_0^{\\pi / 2} \\sin x d x=\\frac{\\frac{\\pi}{2}-0}{4}\\left(\\sin 0+\\sin \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)+2 \\sin \\left(\\frac{0+\\frac{\\pi}{2}}{2}\\right)\\right)=\\frac{\\pi}{8}(1+\\sqrt{2})$.",
    "image": null
  },
